+1. **Guard generator** (design-time) — analyzes a system and produces guards tailored to its entropy profile. Run when setting up guards for a new system or re-evaluating whether existing guards still fit. In this repo today, the assessment workflow rooted at `skills/entropy-assessment/` (and, for the strongest validated case, `skills/docs-first-planning-assessment/`) analyses the system, and `skills/session-coherence-skill-generator/` is the one skill that writes guards.
 
 2. **Guard integrator** (adoption-time) — examines the system's current loops (agent sessions, commits, PRs, CI, releases) and recommends how generated guards should be discovered, triggered, and introduced with minimal friction. This is the bridge between guard design and real use. A generated guard without an adoption path is only half-finished. In this repo, that role is represented by `skills/guards-integrator/SKILL.md`.
 
